\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. \cf0  O God my sins are so heavy,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 many and burdensome.
\par O where can I have a Saviour?
\par There's no helper for me.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2.   If I decide to run away
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 to somewhere far away;
\par and go away from these troubles,
\par shall never stop my woes.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3.   I call to you Lord everyday,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 have pity, turn to me;
\par And lead me not into judgment,
\par You intercede for me.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4.  If it is right to suffer for
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 the price of all my sins;
\par go on and take good care of me
\par protect me ever there.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5.  My God let me be very calm
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 and be a humble man
\par Do never let me think evil
\par To mar my day of grace.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6.  What ever is good in thy sight
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 give to me I will take;
\par the joy of heaven that I plaed,
\par to be my dwelling place.
\par \pard\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs14 
\par }

